Subject: Conditional Panel in the Sidebar Panel

Hi Joe,

My question is similar to this discussion , although I could not figure out exact solution to my specific case; hence I am writing to you instead of starting off a new thread.
I am writing part of the code below-

c1<-c("16681","16892","18586","18921","18923","19731","19775","20275","20965","22873")
c2<-c("20267","24093","24095","25386","25359","25388","25396","25397")

shinyUI(pageWithSidebar(

  headerPanel("Testing & Debugging"),

 sidebarPanel(
  selectInput(
    "SITE_NO", "CenterID",
    c(c1,c2)),

  conditionalPanel(
    condition = "'input.SITE_NO' %in% 'c1'",
    selectInput(
      "WEEK_NO", "Batch",
      c("1","34"))),

    conditionalPanel(
      condition = "'input.SITE_NO' %in% 'c2'" ,
      selectInput("WEEK_NO", "Batch", c("1","34","37"))
  )
),
  mainPanel( )

  ))

What I desire is that WEEK_NO ("1","34") to be displayed when SITE_NO belongs to list c1 and that WEEK_NO ("1","34","37") to be displayed when SITE_NO selected is from the list c2. Currently, I get both the WEEK_NO drop downs.
Thanks in advance.

