Huidong, the problem is that at the time that the inputTracking.js code runs, the controls you want aren't part of the page yet. This is a common problem in jQuery, the solution is to use delegated events <http://api.jquery.com/on/> (scroll down to the section entitled "Direct and delegated events" and read it carefully).

I've created a fork for you that demonstrates this, as well as simplifying the event handling logic:

https://gist.github.com/jcheng5/8441665

