I have re-written my multi-page app to use navbarPage. While it works very nicely it does seem that pages build quite slowly when first visited, especially in Firefox . See for example, Regression > Linear (OLS) at the link below (may need to hit refresh first).

http://vnijs.rady.ucsd.edu:3838/marketing/

I had (mostly) the same functions in the previous version of my app that used a navbar binding by Joe Cheng and it builds pages much faster (see link below):

http://vnijs.rady.ucsd.edu:3838/marketing_fall2013/

I have tried different approaches in my code but have not been able to achieve much of a speed up. Code is here: https://github.com/mostly-harmless/radiant
I tried profiling the app in Chrome and it seems a good fraction of the execution time is spent in the function isHidden in shiny.js. I assume this function influences what pages are (not) shown. Is there any way to achieve a speed-up here?

