Hi Joe,

I love the progress bar you've added, but I had some trouble customizing the location of the bar. I wanted the bar to display in the center of the plot, but these two lines seemed to be overriding any changes I made to progress.css:

 $progress.css('top', (20 * num) + 'px');
 $progress.css('right', (20 * num) + 'px');

No matter what I put in the style sheet, the bar, upon inspection, would have top: 20px; right: 20px;  My solution was to delete those two lines and then modify the css to look like this:

.shiny-progress {
  position: absolute;
  width: 35%;
  top: 30%;
  right: 20%;
  padding: 12px;
  border: 1px solid #CCC;
  border-radius: 8px;
  background-color: #f5f5f5;
  opacity: 0.9;
}

This works for me, but I'm wondering if I just misunderstood the .js code, or missed some other option for positioning?

Thanks.

