As Michael mentioned, the official solution to the problem is Shiny Server Pro <http://www.rstudio.com/shiny/server/>, which has built-in support for SSL <http://rstudio.github.io/shiny-server/latest/#ssl> (example <http://rstudio.github.io/shiny-server/latest/#host-a-secure-shiny-server>) and user-authentication. It also does the password hashing for you (using scrypt) if you use the Flat-File authentication system <http://rstudio.github.io/shiny-server/latest/#flat-file-authentication> (LDAP and Active Directory are also available, if you're in an organization that uses those).

Jeff

